  {
   "id": 532784,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "As an artist, you want to design a cylindrical container for your colored art pencils and another rectangular container for some other tools. The cylindrical container will be 8 inches high with a diameter of 6 inches. The rectangular container measures 10 inches wide by 8 inches deep by 4 inches high and has a lid. You found some beautiful patterned paper to use to wrap both pieces. How much paper will you need?\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/7771bc25ab556f7f.png\" alt=\"A cylinder and a prism. The diameter and height of the cylinder are marked 6 inches and 8 inches. The length, width, and height of the rectangular prism are marked 10 inches, 8 inches, and 4 inches.\">\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Step 1: Find the surface area of the cylinder.</p>\n<p>The surface area of a right cylinder with radius <i>r</i> and height <i>h</i> is <span data-math=\"SA = 2\\pi {r^2} + 2\\pi rh\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"SA = 2\\pi {r^2} + 2\\pi rh = 2\\pi {\\left( {{\\text{3 in}}} \\right)^2} + 2\\pi \\left( {{\\text{3 in}}} \\right)\\left( {{\\text{8 in}}} \\right) \\approx 207.345{\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: Find the surface area of the right prism.</p>\n<p>The surface area of a right prism where <i>B</i> is the area of the base, <i>p</i> is the perimeter of the base, and <i>h</i> is the height is <span data-math=\"SA = 2B + ph\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The rectangular base has an area <span data-math=\"{\\text{ =  LW  =  (10 in) (8 in)  =  80 i}}{{\\text{n}}^{\\text{2}}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The perimeter of the base <span data-math=\"{\\text{ =  }}p{\\text{  =  2(10 in)  +  2(8 in)  =  36 cm}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The surface area <span data-math=\"= {\\text{ }}2B + ph = {\\text{ }}2\\left( {80{\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^2}} \\right){\\text{ }} + {\\text{ }}\\left( {36{\\text{ in}}} \\right)\\left( {4{\\text{ in}}} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}160{\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^2} + {\\text{ }}144{\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^2} = {\\text{ }}304{\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Step 3: Add the results of the previous two steps.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"207.35{\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^2} + {\\text{ }}304{\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^2} = {\\text{ }}511.35{\\text{ i}}{{\\text{n}}^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>The total area is 511.35 square inches.</p>\n"
    },
    {
